      "notes": "Listings: msigner layout (two 600-sat dummies, seller 0x83 at vin 2, payment vout 2, fee vout 3; N items use N+1 dummies and one fee output after the last payment); rare sats were whole-UTXO listings on the same flow. Rune listings use no dummies, so the seller's sats reach the buyer's change or the miner, not the item output. Accepted offers and bids: the seller signs ALL (often an explicit 0x01) or DEFAULT at acceptance, [item vin 0] -> [item vout 0, payment vout 1, fee vout 2, change], sometimes with the bid escrowed in a P2WSH input. Not sales: 1,000-sat transfer-tool fees, launchpad mints, inscription commits, fee-wallet sweeps.",
